nection with the arrangements David made for the building of the temple (2 Sam. 7:2, 3, 17), and next appears as the reprover of David on account of his sin with Bathsheba (12:1-14).","verses":29,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1,5,7,13,15,25]},{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[8]},{"id":"uriah_2898","name":"Uriah","also":"Urias","summary":"A Hittite, the husband of Bathsheba, whom David first seduced, and then after Uriah’s death married. He was one of the band of David’s “mighty men.”","verses":22,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9,10,15]},{"id":"solomon_2762","name":"Solomon","also":"Jedidiah","summary":"Peaceful, (Heb. Shelomoh), David’s second son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[24,25]},{"id":"bathsheba_416","name":"Bathsheba","also":"Bath-sheba, Bath-shua","summary":"Daughter of the oath, or of seven, called also Bath-shu’a (1 Chr. 3:5), was the daughter of Eliam (2 Sam. 11:3) or Ammiel (1 Chr. 3:5), and wife of Uriah the Hittite.","verses":11,"father":"Eliam","mother":"","v":[24]},{"id":"joab_1617","name":"Joab","also":"","summary":"One of the three sons of Zeruiah, David’s sister, and “captain of the host” during the whole of David’s reign (2 Sam. 2:13; 10:7; 11:1; 1 Kings 11:15).","verses":119,"father":"","mother":"Zeruiah","v":[26,27]}],"places":[{"id":"rabbah_966","name":"Rabbah","kind":"","lat":31.95522,"lon":35.94503,"summary":"“Rabbath of the children of Ammon,” the chief city of the Ammonites, among the eastern hills, some 20 miles east of the Jordan, on the southern of the two streams which united with the Jabbok.","verses":14,"v":[26,27,29]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “h